  {
    "id": 86,
    "time": "2024-09-21T18:08:40.700Z",
    "channel": "STABLE",
    "commits": [
      {
        "sha": "9c450388e10f4b6669dd6f039de953927899b3bc",
        "time": "2024-09-21T17:57:08Z",
        "message": "Return null in getRegistry(Class) for unknown type (#11422)\n\nThe Bukkit#getRegistry(Class) method contract specifies that it returns\r\nnull for unknown registry types. The current implementation however\r\nrequires the passed class to be mappable to a known registry key.\r\n\r\nFor types like Material, which have a SimpleRegistry in bukkit's\r\nRegistry interface, no server side registry exists and such the type\r\ncannot be mapped to a registry key.\r\n\r\nThe commit correctly returns null for types that are not mappable to a\r\nregistry key instead of throwing a NullPointerException."
      }
    ],
    "downloads": {
      "server:default": {
        "name": "paper-1.21.1-86.jar",
        "checksums": {
          "sha256": "9330a93713a3579b9b91b5ddaa2ffa39fc950cdae55414d6f14a270e7464bef5"
        },
        "size": 49324331,
        "url": "https://fill-data.papermc.io/v1/objects/9330a93713a3579b9b91b5ddaa2ffa39fc950cdae55414d6f14a270e7464bef5/paper-1.21.1-86.jar"
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "id": 85,
    "time": "2024-09-19T14:49:51.160Z",
    "channel": "STABLE",
    "commits": [
      {
        "sha": "c5a10665b8b80af650500b9263036f778f06d500",
        "time": "2024-09-19T14:36:07Z",
        "message": "Remove wall-time / unused skip tick protection (#11412)\n\nSpigot still maintains some partial implementation of \"tick skipping\", a\npractice in which the MinecraftServer.currentTick field is updated not\nby an increment of one per actual tick, but instead set to\nSystem.currentTimeMillis() / 50. This behaviour means that the tracked\ntick may \"skip\" a tick value in case a previous tick took more than the\nexpected 50ms.\n\nTo compensate for this in important paths, spigot/craftbukkit\nimplements \"wall-time\". Instead of incrementing/decrementing ticks on\nblock entities/entities by one for each call to their tick() method,\nthey instead increment/decrement important values, like\nan ItemEntity's age or pickupDelay, by the difference of\n`currentTick - lastTick`, where `lastTick` is the value of\n`currentTick` during the last tick() call.\n\nThese \"fixes\" however do not play nicely with minecraft's simulation\ndistance as entities/block entities implementing the above behaviour\nwould \"catch up\" their values when moving from a non-ticking chunk to a\nticking one as their `lastTick` value remains stuck on the last tick in\na ticking chunk and hence lead to a large \"catch up\" once ticked again.\n\nPaper completely removes the \"tick skipping\" behaviour (See patch\n\"Further-improve-server-tick-loop\"), making the above precautions\ncompletely unnecessary, which also rids paper of the previous described\nincompatibility with non-ticking chunks.\n"
      }
    ],
    "downloads": {
      "server:default": {
        "name": "paper-1.21.1-85.jar",
        "checksums": {
          "sha256": "987698cc5efd3f1bf6eea671711cdc9d2286b9a684c9b013409a3ea401e8c899"
        },
        "size": 49326339,
        "url": "https://fill-data.papermc.io/v1/objects/987698cc5efd3f1bf6eea671711cdc9d2286b9a684c9b013409a3ea401e8c899/paper-1.21.1-85.jar"
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "id": 84,
    "time": "2024-09-19T14:38:58.293Z",
    "channel": "STABLE",
    "commits": [
      {
        "sha": "5c829557332f21b34bc81e6ad1a73e511faef8f6",
        "time": "2024-09-19T14:27:33Z",
        "message": "Only mark decorations dirty if a removal actually occurs (#11413)\n\n* Only mark decorations dirty if a removal actually occurs\n\nVanilla calls this method blindly inside of a loop which erroniously marks\nmap data files as being dirty even if nothing has actually changed.\n\n* Merge into existing patch\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Bjarne Koll \u003Clynxplay101@gmail.com\u003E"
      }
    ],
