  {
    "id": 82,
    "time": "2024-09-16T19:04:41.734Z",
    "channel": "STABLE",
    "commits": [
      {
        "sha": "1348e44173f422a7bf6f162a28c70a229dfe827b",
        "time": "2024-09-16T18:53:00Z",
        "message": "Prevent NPE when serializing unresolved profile (#11407)\n\nIn the recent upstream update, the paper player profile was updated to\r\ncorrectly return null for both name and id if constructed as such. This\r\nchange however broke the serialisation logic, as it depended on the name\r\nnever being null.\r\n\r\nThe commit moves the checks over to the newly introduced emptyName/UUID\r\nfields that track if the profile was constructed with a null name or\r\nuuid to differentiate it against an empty string or the NIL_UUID."
      }
    ],
